<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madang</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Friedrich-Wilhelmshafen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madang is a port town on the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papua-new-guinea">Papua New Guinea</a>. Founded by the Germans as Friedrich-Wilhelmshafen, it was the seat of the German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> Company's administration in the 1890s. Occupied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> in 1914 and by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> from 1942 to 1944, it is now the capital of Madang Province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/madang.jpg" alt="Madang" width="225" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nomadtales at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Madang_Lighthouse.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
